WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:11.810 --> 00:00:14.510
The former chief executive
of Wirecard, Marcus Braun,

00:00:14.510 --> 00:00:15.483
has been arrested.

00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:19.420
Auditors revealed that nearly $2 billion

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:21.680
has gone missing.

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:23.640
This has been a wild ride for Wirecard.

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:24.770
You only need to look at the share price

00:00:24.770 --> 00:00:26.153
over the past five days.

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:29.950
Wirecard is a payment processing company.

00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:33.193
At their height they were
worth 22 billion euros.

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:38.220
Wirecard was supposed
to be Germany's ticket

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:40.000
into the high-tech world.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.480
They were supposed to be
the pride of German fintech.

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:46.500
Wirecard spectacularly imploded.

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:50.330
Its stock went to penny stock
level and now it's worthless.

00:00:50.330 --> 00:00:51.520
That is quite remarkable.

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:56.030
Never before has a company on
Germany's DAX just gone bust.

00:00:56.030 --> 00:00:58.450
Is there a corporate fraud going on here

00:00:58.450 --> 00:01:00.630
or is it something more mundane?

00:01:00.630 --> 00:01:03.120
The business model was fraudulent right

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:03.953
from the beginning.

00:01:03.953 --> 00:01:07.140
It was bank robbery and
investors and creditors

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:11.510
they're seeking more than 12
billion euros in repayments.

00:01:11.510 --> 00:01:13.450
The two key players are two Austrians.

00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:15.850
The chief executive, Markus Braun

00:01:15.850 --> 00:01:18.170
and his deputy, Jan Marsalek.

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:20.070
Right now, Marcus Braun is in jail

00:01:20.070 --> 00:01:21.250
and he's facing charges.

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:24.410
It's far more difficult to know
anything about Jan Marsalek

00:01:24.410 --> 00:01:25.450
because he's missing.

00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:27.890
There is reason to believe
that he had close ties

00:01:27.890 --> 00:01:30.160
to secret services around the world,

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:33.740
so he had the means
and obviously the money

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:36.060
to just vanish without a trace.

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:38.590
Might he be in Russia?
Might he be in Asia?

00:01:38.590 --> 00:01:42.430
Might he be on some deserted
island? Nobody really knows.

00:01:42.430 --> 00:01:44.560
He's on the most wanted list of Interpol,

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:47.353
but so far, nobody's been
able to track him down.

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:59.500
The German economy mostly
builds on car-makers

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:02.660
and engineering companies,
which is sort of the past.

00:02:02.660 --> 00:02:06.650
Wirecard was that bright
new future-oriented company

00:02:06.650 --> 00:02:09.470
and Wirecard promised
that they would deliver

00:02:09.470 --> 00:02:12.350
electronic payments and in the future

00:02:12.350 --> 00:02:13.970
they would become a super big company.

00:02:13.970 --> 00:02:16.420
They started as a startup, essentially,

00:02:16.420 --> 00:02:21.032
around 2000 and grew up around
the, you know, what some

00:02:21.032 --> 00:02:23.740
people might find, slightly
unappetizing businesses

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:26.790
of pornographic content and gambling

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:29.820
and then turned themselves
into a main player

00:02:29.820 --> 00:02:33.320
in the global payment
facilitation business.

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:36.060
Markus, when you look at Wirecard's

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:38.800
share price, it's eye-watering.

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:40.700
The incredible acceleration

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:42.360
in the valuation of your business.

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:44.210
I think we are showing enormous growth,

00:02:44.210 --> 00:02:47.070
I have no fear at all
in terms of evaluation.

00:02:47.070 --> 00:02:51.610
Starting in 2010, Wirecard's
profits began to explode

00:02:51.610 --> 00:02:53.790
and show a very, very solid

00:02:53.790 --> 00:02:56.470
and almost too good to believe growth.

00:02:56.470 --> 00:02:59.300
Wirecard at some point replaced
Germany's second largest

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:04.100
lender, Commerzbank, and its
market value of over 22 billion

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:06.690
was more than Deutsche
Bank, the biggest lender,

00:03:06.690 --> 00:03:11.000
and Commerzbank combined.
Which showed the significance

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:13.980
and how things have changed
in the German economy.

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:16.780
There's a chap called Jan Marsalek,

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:19.050
who was the chief operating officer.

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:22.400
There is another guy called
Markus Braun, the CEO.

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:24.310
And while we know some elements

00:03:24.310 --> 00:03:28.400
of what led to the fall of this company,

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:30.420
there were some elements
that we didn't know about.

00:03:30.420 --> 00:03:33.270
I met Jan Marsalek just
for a background chat,

00:03:33.270 --> 00:03:35.210
and he was quite frank about his youth,

00:03:35.210 --> 00:03:39.590
that he was mostly interested
in IT and programming.

00:03:39.590 --> 00:03:41.800
I can only assume he was a classical nerd

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:42.780
when he was younger.

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:45.270
When he rose through
the ranks at Wirecard,

00:03:45.270 --> 00:03:47.810
he developed a taste for the extravagant.

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:50.400
He lived the life of a high roller,

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:52.070
looking back he spent more money

00:03:52.070 --> 00:03:54.573
than what he was earning
as a Wirecard executive.

00:04:00.890 --> 00:04:03.860
Jan Marsalek was close to a commander

00:04:03.860 --> 00:04:07.170
of a Russian mercenary army
who took him to the Syrian city

00:04:07.170 --> 00:04:11.520
of Palmyra right after
that Russian mercenary army

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:14.520
expelled ISIL from the city.

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:16.610
He flew in there, he went to the beach

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:18.940
and fired around Kalashnikovs I was told.

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:23.430
He even took a small piece of
an ornament back to Germany.

00:04:23.430 --> 00:04:25.140
I saw it, I held it in my own hands.

00:04:25.140 --> 00:04:29.200
Part of the Wirecard
story that we've uncovered

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:32.910
is a little bit sort of
boys' fantasies - you know

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:37.903
men in expensive suits and fancy
watches, champagne parties.

00:04:40.023 --> 00:04:42.800
Investors are impressed,
Markus, by the growth.

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:46.410
If you look of the last 15
years your up 40,000 percent.

00:04:46.410 --> 00:04:48.320
Interestingly, the collapse of Wirecard

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:51.820
starts around the time where
Wirecard is at its peak.

00:04:51.820 --> 00:04:54.470
And that is when they
joined the DAX Index.

00:04:54.470 --> 00:04:56.770
And that's really a huge achievement

00:04:56.770 --> 00:05:00.310
to be among the 30 biggest
companies of Germany.

00:05:00.310 --> 00:05:03.330
At their height, its
market value was at 20,

00:05:03.330 --> 00:05:05.903
22 and a half billion euros.

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:11.710
The illegitimate part of
Wirecard was, in large parts,

00:05:11.710 --> 00:05:14.610
a business that happened
far away from headquarters.

00:05:14.610 --> 00:05:17.240
So these were businesses that were in Asia

00:05:17.240 --> 00:05:19.500
or in the Middle East, businesses largely

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:22.560
where Wirecard had no
sort of operating license

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:24.990
of its own and, therefore,
relied on partners

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:25.823
to work with them.

00:05:25.823 --> 00:05:28.100
Unknown to the public and wider audience,

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:31.150
Wirecard faked profits and transactions.

00:05:31.150 --> 00:05:32.480
How did they do this?

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:34.500
They had a business that was called

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:36.320
third party providing business.

00:05:36.320 --> 00:05:38.950
They did business with outside partners

00:05:38.950 --> 00:05:41.810
that processed transactions in countries

00:05:41.810 --> 00:05:43.160
where they had no license.

00:05:43.160 --> 00:05:45.250
And these businesses provided Wirecard

00:05:45.250 --> 00:05:47.570
with fake profit statements

00:05:47.570 --> 00:05:49.730
and fake balance sheet statements.

00:05:49.730 --> 00:05:52.340
Wirecard in reality
didn't turn out a profit.

00:05:52.340 --> 00:05:55.090
If you stripped the profits
from the fake business

00:05:55.090 --> 00:05:59.140
which provided fake revenue
and profit statements,

00:05:59.140 --> 00:06:02.460
it was unprofitable at least since 2016.

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:06.183
Basically the entire
company was a smoke screen.

00:06:08.060 --> 00:06:09.917
The trouble of the way Wirecard was set up

00:06:09.917 --> 00:06:12.720
was that nobody, or very few people,

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:15.720
had a global overview of the company.

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:17.800
A lot of people knew a little sliver.

00:06:17.800 --> 00:06:21.030
The auditors, Ernst &amp; Young, for years,

00:06:21.030 --> 00:06:22.610
signed off on their accounts.

00:06:22.610 --> 00:06:24.330
And so there doesn't seem to
be anything untoward there.

00:06:24.330 --> 00:06:26.800
There didn't seem to be
anything illegitimate,

00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:29.420
but the questions kept coming,

00:06:29.420 --> 00:06:30.890
particularly from the Financial Times

00:06:30.890 --> 00:06:34.240
that started publishing
reports around 2018

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:37.500
saying that there were problems
with accounting in Asia.

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:39.277
And every turn Wirecard said,

00:06:39.277 --> 00:06:41.810
"No, this is not true,
this is legitimate."

00:06:41.810 --> 00:06:44.600
They often would raise their forecasts

00:06:44.600 --> 00:06:46.950
as to appeal investors

00:06:46.950 --> 00:06:49.670
and they managed to wiggle
out of this, time and again.

00:06:49.670 --> 00:06:53.430
Let me ask about the scandals

00:06:53.430 --> 00:06:54.960
that we've seen in the stock market.

00:06:54.960 --> 00:06:58.620
I do not, too much,
look into controversies.

00:06:58.620 --> 00:07:01.570
In the Philippines, they had
an account with two banks

00:07:01.570 --> 00:07:04.340
on which about $2 billion were sitting.

00:07:04.340 --> 00:07:07.610
It got from the bank fake
balance sheet confirmations,

00:07:07.610 --> 00:07:10.890
and this is how the entire
smoke screen worked.

00:07:10.890 --> 00:07:12.730
There did, however, come a point

00:07:12.730 --> 00:07:16.330
around the time of 2019, 2020,

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:19.210
where they enlisted the
help of a second auditor,

00:07:19.210 --> 00:07:20.307
and that was KPMG.

00:07:20.307 --> 00:07:24.550
And KPMG was asked for a
special audit of the books.

00:07:24.550 --> 00:07:26.460
They flew down to Manila

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:29.800
and initially nobody
doubted the money was there.

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:33.070
They just wanted to see, can
this be tapped at any time,

00:07:33.070 --> 00:07:34.460
is this free liquidity?

00:07:34.460 --> 00:07:38.400
What we now know is that a
lot of this was fictitious,

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:41.370
that some documents were outright forged,

00:07:41.370 --> 00:07:43.290
that some employees at these banks

00:07:43.290 --> 00:07:45.700
were not who they said they would be.

00:07:45.700 --> 00:07:48.210
Knowing now that this money never existed,

00:07:48.210 --> 00:07:51.960
that obviously posed a huge
problem for Jan Marsalek,

00:07:51.960 --> 00:07:54.880
who was faced with a
daunting task of coming up

00:07:54.880 --> 00:07:56.940
with several hundred millions of euros

00:07:56.940 --> 00:07:59.520
that he could transfer
from Asia to Europe.

00:07:59.520 --> 00:08:01.590
As we know, that never happened.

00:08:01.590 --> 00:08:04.150
And that was sort of the
beginning of the end of Wirecard,

00:08:04.150 --> 00:08:04.983
as we know it.

00:08:04.983 --> 00:08:06.330
The scandal that has been brewing

00:08:06.330 --> 00:08:09.510
over the last week is
now definitely deepening.

00:08:09.510 --> 00:08:12.110
The initial employees said no money,

00:08:12.110 --> 00:08:16.080
none of Wirecard's missing 2.1 billion

00:08:16.080 --> 00:08:17.800
ever entered into the Philippines.

00:08:17.800 --> 00:08:19.570
The company has temporarily suspended

00:08:19.570 --> 00:08:21.153
its outgoing COO, Jan Marsalek,

00:08:22.150 --> 00:08:23.780
but it seems there will
be further questions

00:08:23.780 --> 00:08:24.667
for the business to answer.

00:08:24.667 --> 00:08:27.549
Jan Marsalek was suspended on June 18.

00:08:27.549 --> 00:08:30.500
Marsalek went into Braun's
office for one last time

00:08:30.500 --> 00:08:35.210
and someone who happened
to stumble into the room

00:08:35.210 --> 00:08:37.280
said there were intense discussions.

00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:40.380
Braun kept talking at Marsalek,

00:08:40.380 --> 00:08:43.173
and soon thereafter Marsalek went missing.

00:08:44.350 --> 00:08:46.440
We're looking at a space of a week,

00:08:46.440 --> 00:08:50.230
from Marsalek existing Wirecard HQ

00:08:50.230 --> 00:08:52.870
to Wirecard going up in smoke.

00:08:52.870 --> 00:08:55.190
More details on this to come, but again,

00:08:55.190 --> 00:08:57.860
a clearly unusual scandal.

00:08:57.860 --> 00:08:59.210
In some ways, Jan Marsalek

00:08:59.210 --> 00:09:01.400
is sort of a mirror image of Wirecard.

00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:04.850
There is the visible, the legal part,

00:09:04.850 --> 00:09:07.270
if you want, of Jan Marsalek,

00:09:07.270 --> 00:09:09.270
which is he's the chief operating officer

00:09:09.270 --> 00:09:10.970
of a large German company,

00:09:10.970 --> 00:09:15.060
and then there is the murkier,
opaque part of Jan Marsalek,

00:09:15.060 --> 00:09:18.973
which is dealing with
mercenaries, traveling to Syria.

00:09:21.010 --> 00:09:24.300
There is one place where
it's easy to get a sense

00:09:24.300 --> 00:09:26.910
of who Wirecard and Marsalek was,

00:09:26.910 --> 00:09:28.850
and that is this opulent villa

00:09:28.850 --> 00:09:30.490
that sits in the middle of Munich.

00:09:30.490 --> 00:09:34.880
This is a place where Jan
Marsalek had his residence.

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:36.660
He didn't formally live there,

00:09:36.660 --> 00:09:40.270
but he had all the fripperies
that you might want.

00:09:40.270 --> 00:09:42.080
I was granted access to the building

00:09:42.080 --> 00:09:43.913
by someone who was authorized

00:09:46.226 --> 00:09:48.140
and I developed my own little
obsession of finding out

00:09:48.140 --> 00:09:48.973
what was going on.

00:09:48.973 --> 00:09:51.530
There's a room with some artwork,

00:09:51.530 --> 00:09:55.170
but it also has that kind of
appearance now of being a place

00:09:55.170 --> 00:09:58.030
that was hastily and quickly abandoned.

00:09:58.030 --> 00:10:01.910
Most of the furniture was
removed from the place

00:10:01.910 --> 00:10:06.070
but there was still two
intensive care bed units.

00:10:06.070 --> 00:10:09.130
In the basement, there was a huge locker

00:10:09.130 --> 00:10:14.130
with drugs inside uppers,
downers, stimulants.

00:10:16.262 --> 00:10:18.970
Its quite extraordinary to have 2 billion

00:10:18.970 --> 00:10:21.430
lost and not know where it is.

00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:24.900
I was told that Marsalek and his gang

00:10:24.900 --> 00:10:28.810
funneled out 1.5 billion of the company.

00:10:28.810 --> 00:10:31.590
We know he milked the company dry

00:10:31.590 --> 00:10:35.670
by transferring a lot of loans
that the company provided

00:10:35.670 --> 00:10:39.360
to entities that he then
secretly controlled abroad.

00:10:39.360 --> 00:10:40.990
Investors and creditors,

00:10:40.990 --> 00:10:45.168
they're seeking more than 12
billion euros in repayments.

00:10:45.168 --> 00:10:47.200
How can a error, a mistake,

00:10:47.200 --> 00:10:51.620
a scandal of that size,
happen in a DAX corporation.

00:10:51.620 --> 00:10:53.930
We have many questions that
we want to ask the government

00:10:53.930 --> 00:10:54.960
in the following weeks.

00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:57.160
These guys, these companies
have auditors, right?

00:10:57.160 --> 00:10:59.440
Is it time to audit the auditors?

00:10:59.440 --> 00:11:02.660
The decline of Wirecard is
obviously a huge embarrassment

00:11:02.660 --> 00:11:04.570
for a lot of constituencies out there.

00:11:04.570 --> 00:11:07.010
There are the auditors, who signed off

00:11:07.010 --> 00:11:08.410
on these accounts for years.

00:11:08.410 --> 00:11:10.630
And the question that's out there

00:11:10.630 --> 00:11:12.460
and that remains unanswered is,

00:11:12.460 --> 00:11:15.350
why did they not detect what was going on?

00:11:15.350 --> 00:11:17.920
I mean, Ernst &amp; Young is
one of the big auditors.

00:11:17.920 --> 00:11:20.610
They should know what's
going on at these companies.

00:11:20.610 --> 00:11:25.360
This company had all kinds
of signs, reported by media

00:11:25.360 --> 00:11:27.160
going back a year or two now

00:11:27.160 --> 00:11:29.690
and yet people still gave
the company the benefit

00:11:29.690 --> 00:11:31.840
of the doubt, over and
over and over again.

00:11:33.240 --> 00:11:37.040
How did Wirecard get so
much political support?

00:11:37.040 --> 00:11:38.770
The prosecutors have for a long time

00:11:38.770 --> 00:11:40.880
turned a blind eye on Wirecard,

00:11:40.880 --> 00:11:44.980
and for the entire institution
apparatus of Germany,

00:11:44.980 --> 00:11:46.270
it is very embarrassing.

00:11:46.270 --> 00:11:49.380
Investors, first and
foremost, have lost out here.

00:11:49.380 --> 00:11:53.060
And among the investors, spare
a thought for Marcus Brown,

00:11:53.060 --> 00:11:55.160
who was the biggest
investor in the company

00:11:55.160 --> 00:11:57.780
and he went from billionaire
to now sitting in jail.

00:11:57.780 --> 00:11:59.560
So quite a downfall for him.

00:11:59.560 --> 00:12:01.860
Most people might not
have too much sympathy,

00:12:01.860 --> 00:12:04.993
but if we speak of losers,
he's certainly among them.

00:12:05.930 --> 00:12:10.810
Wirecard was fraud probably
right from the beginning.

00:12:10.810 --> 00:12:13.320
It's the biggest financial
scandal in Germany.

00:12:13.320 --> 00:12:15.030
And the amount of money that was lost,

00:12:15.030 --> 00:12:17.110
it was probably the biggest bank robbery

00:12:17.110 --> 00:12:18.610
that happened in this country.

